  {
   "x": 5,
   "y": 1,
   "plaque": "arts_jack_yeats",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "Jack B. Yeats",
   "text": "Jack Butler Yeats, the poet's younger brother, was born in London in 1871 and grew up here in Sligo with his grandparents, the Pollexfens. He drew horses, boxers, tinkers and the sea, then painted the west in thick, loud colour that nobody taught him. At the 1924 Paris Olympics, when art had medals, his painting The Liffey Swim won silver: the Irish Free State's first Olympic medal. Samuel Beckett came to his studio and never forgot it. He died in 1957. The Niland Collection here holds the best of him, and the rain outside is in the right colours."
  }
